{
  "name": "Draft cashwerk invoices from won deals",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## How it works\nA won deal becomes a draft invoice for the same customer, so the first billable moment is captured while the deal is still fresh. The invoice is created as a draft: a person still opens it, adds the lines and sends it.\n\nThe cashwerk Trigger subscribes to **deal.update** and the first IF reads *completionStatus* out of the event body, which costs no API call. Only a won deal is read back in full, because the customer sits on a many-to-many relation the event body does not carry. The second IF is the part worth keeping: an invoice needs a billing address, which comes from the customer, so a deal with no contact is skipped instead of being sent to the API to fail. The invoice carries today's date, the deal title and net pricing.\n\n## Setup steps\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-cashwerk** (Settings → Community nodes).\n2. In cashwerk go to **Settings → API Platform** and create an API key with read access to deals and write access to invoices. Add it as a **cashwerk API** credential on all three cashwerk nodes — the trigger, *Get Deal* and *Create Invoice*.\n3. Activate the workflow. The trigger registers the webhook in cashwerk by itself.\n4. Mark a test deal as won and open the draft it produces.\n\n## Customisation\n- Change `netGross` to `gross` on *Create Invoice* for gross pricing.\n- Take the customer from the deal's company instead by using `companies[0].id` with `clientType: \"COMPANY\"`.",
        "height": 643,
        "width": 860,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1020,
        -150
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The deal is won\nSubscribes to deal.update and lets only completionStatus = WON through. The event body carries the deal columns, so this costs no API call.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-s1",
      "name": "Section 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -70,
        -150
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Find the customer\nThe deal is read back in full because the contact sits on a many-to-many relation the webhook body does not carry. An invoice needs a billing address, which comes from the customer, so a deal without a contact is skipped here rather than failing at the API.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-s2",
      "name": "Section 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        370,
        -150
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Draft the invoice\nCreates a draft with today's date, the deal title and net pricing. Lines and sending stay with a person.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-s3",
      "name": "Section 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        810,
        -150
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "events": [
          "deal.update"
        ]
      },
      "id": "node-1",
      "name": "cashwerk Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-cashwerk.cashwerkTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "cashwerkApi": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "cashwerk account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
